{
  "$schema": "com.minomobi.cad.assembly#v1",
  "name": "clock",
  "_": "The clock. A going train of three stages from the escape wheel to the centre arbor (8:60, 8:32, 8:32 = 120:1), so one-second beats give a minute hand at one turn an hour; a lever escapement — escape wheel, pallet fork, balance — as the drive, stepping the wheel half a tooth per beat; motion works (12:36 then 8:32 = 12:1) to the hour hand; a dial with twelve marks; the case. Gear phases are automatic. Every part is a bench tree with parameter overrides. Riding parts (hour wheel, hour hand) have 0.1 mm of clearance on the arbor; fixed parts are a press fit, which the interference check reports as fixed-mated touches.",
